# Salt Software - Cursor Rules

You are a Senior Engineer working on Salt, a client management platform for creative agencies.

**Dual harness:** Cursor is primary; Claude Code (`.claude/`) is backup. Shared standards live in `CLAUDE.md` + nested `CLAUDE.md` files. Full guide: `docs/guides/dual-agent-setup.md`.

## Context-Aware Rules System

This project uses **nested context rules** (like Claude Code's CLAUDE.md files). Rules auto-load based on which files you're editing:

| Directory | Rule File | Context |
|-----------|-----------|---------|
| `app/**` | `01-app.mdc` | App Router patterns |
| `app/_features/**` | `02-features.mdc` | Feature modules |
| `app/_lib/**` | `03-lib.mdc` | Infrastructure |
| `packages/ui/**` | `04-packages-ui.mdc` | shadcn/ui primitives |
| `supabase/**` | `05-supabase.mdc` | Database & RLS |
| `e2e/**` | `06-e2e.mdc` | Playwright testing |
| `packages/**` | `07-packages.mdc` | Shared libraries |
| `brand-identity/**` | `08-brand-identity.mdc` | Brand & voice |
| `docs/**` | `09-docs.mdc` | Documentation |

**These rules are in `.cursor/rules/` and apply automatically.**

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15.1.9 (App Router)
- **UI**: React 19, TypeScript 5.9.3, Tailwind CSS 4
- **Backend**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Storage), Stripe
- **Testing**: Vitest (unit), Playwright (E2E) — NEVER Jest, NEVER Cypress
- **Package Manager**: pnpm — NEVER npm, NEVER yarn

## Critical Commands

```bash
# Development
pnpm dev:op          # Start dev server (1Password secrets)
pnpm dev             # Start dev server (.env.local fallback)
pnpm build           # Production build
pnpm lint --fix      # Lint and auto-fix

# Testing
pnpm test            # Unit tests (Vitest)
pnpm test:e2e        # E2E tests (Playwright)
pnpm test:e2e --ui   # E2E debug mode

# Dependencies
pnpm install         # Install deps
pnpm add <package>   # Add package
```

**Port 3000 is required** — E2E tests and database configs expect localhost:3000.

## Project Structure

```
app/
├── _features/       # Domain modules (auth, clients, projects, messaging, etc.)
├── _lib/            # Shared utilities (supabase, stripe, security, hooks)
├── (studio)/        # Main app routes (rewritten from app.usesalt.io)
├── (bridge)/        # Client portal routes (rewritten from bridge.usesalt.io)
└── globals.css      # Tailwind config

packages/
├── ui/              # @repo/ui - shadcn/ui primitives
├── patterns/        # @repo/patterns - composed components
└── theme/           # @repo/theme - design tokens

docs/
├── architecture/    # System design docs
├── guides/          # Development guides
└── plans/           # Feature plans (qplan output)

e2e/                 # Playwright E2E tests
supabase/            # Database migrations and seeds
brand-identity/      # Brand voice, positioning, product docs
```

## Non-Negotiable Standards

| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Components | Functional components only. Hooks for state. |
| Styling | Tailwind utility classes. No inline styles. |
| Data Fetching | Use the Data Access Layer (DAL) in `app/_lib/dal/` |
| Error Handling | Server actions return `Result<T, E>` objects |
| Testing | Co-locate unit tests (`*.test.ts`). E2E in `e2e/` (`*.spec.ts`) |
| Locators | E2E uses `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`. No CSS selectors. |
| Types | No `any`. No `@ts-ignore`. No placeholder comments. |

## UI Components

Use `@repo/ui` (shadcn/ui primitives):
```tsx
import { Button } from "@repo/ui/button"
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from "@repo/ui/card"
import { Input } from "@repo/ui/input"
```

Loading states use Lucide icons:
```tsx
import { Loader2 } from "lucide-react"
<Loader2 className="animate-spin" />
```

## Velocity Triggers

| Trigger | Action |
|---------|--------|
| `qplan` | Draft plan to `docs/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>.md`. Don't code yet. |
| `qcode` | Implement approved plan. TDD: test → fail → code → pass. |
| `qtest` | Write/run tests. Unit for logic, E2E for user flows. |
| `qcheck` | Review for security, types, performance, patterns. |
| `qfix` | Analyze error, propose fix. |
| `qcleanup` | Run `code-structure-cleanup` skill after a working feature. |
| `qstructure` | Apply `code-structure` service-layer rules when duplicating logic. |
| `qsource` | Use `source-code-context` — search opensrc / reference repos before guessing APIs. |
| `qreview` | Run `grep-loop-review-workflow` **autonomous loop** — up to 5 rounds: fetch Greptile comments → fix → test → push → re-review. Do not stop after one pass. Add `no-push` or `max N` to override defaults. |
| `qreview-pragmatic` | Run `pragmatic-code-review` — holistic principal-engineer review of branch diff. |
| `qresearch` | Research before building — **provider required** (see below). |
| `qresearch gemini` | Run `gemini-research` — script + synthesis → `brand-identity/research/` (deep pre-build). |
| `qresearch perplexity` | Run `perplexity-research` — Perplexity MCP (`perplexity_ask` / `perplexity_research`). |
| `qdebug` | Run `systematic-debugging` — root cause before any fix. |
| `qux` | Run `frontend-design` + `interaction-patterns` for UI work. |
| `qdb` | Run `database-keeper` — explore / audit / analyze / draft migrations (read `supabase/CLAUDE.md`). |
| `qscout` | Run `ux-scout` — research UX patterns before building a feature. |
| `stripe` | Run `stripe-best-practices` (and `upgrade-stripe` when bumping API/SDK). |

## Agent Skills (`.cursor/skills/`)

Cursor-native skills. Most are also under `.claude/skills/` or `.agents/skills/` for Claude Code.

### Engineering (Tier 1)

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `testing-patterns` | Writing Vitest tests, factories, TDD |
| `systematic-debugging` | Bugs, failures — no fix without root cause |
| `frontend-design` | Building UI with shadcn / `@repo/ui` |
| `webapp-testing` | Playwright dogfooding on localhost:3000 |
| `pragmatic-code-review` | Pre-merge holistic review |
| `code-structure` | Service layer vs actions |
| `code-structure-cleanup` | Post-feature dedup pass |
| `source-code-context` | `pnpm opensrc path` before guessing APIs |
| `grep-loop-review-workflow` | Greptile / review fix loop |
| `database-keeper` | Supabase explore, RLS audit, migration drafts |
| `ux-scout` | UX pattern research before implementation |

### Planning & UX (Tier 2)

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `gemini-research` | Pre-build research via Gemini script + synthesis (`qresearch gemini`) |
| `perplexity-research` | Cited web lookup via Perplexity MCP (`qresearch perplexity`) |
| `deep-research` | Manual research when APIs/MCP unavailable |
| `prd` | Decompose features for parallel execution |
| `product-planning` | Opportunity framing, JTBD, Kano |
| `interaction-patterns` | Motion, hover, loading patterns |
| `react-ui-patterns` | Async UI, loading/error states |

### Product, brand & payments (Tier 3)

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `salt-voice` | Salt product copy (usesalt.io) |
| `brand-voice-extraction` | Client brand voice from samples |
| `stripe-best-practices` | Stripe integration decisions |
| `stripe-projects` | Stripe Projects bootstrap |
| `upgrade-stripe` | API/SDK version upgrades |

**1Password:** Secrets in `.env.1password`. Dev server: `pnpm dev:op`. Gemini script: `pnpm research:op --query "..."`. Cursor + MCP: quit Cursor, then `op run --env-file=.env.1password -- open -a Cursor .` from repo root. Check: `pnpm env:op-check`.

**Greptile:** `greptile` item in vault → `GREPTILE_API_KEY`. MCP in `.mcp.json`. Trigger: `qreview`.

**Research triggers:**

| Trigger | Provider | How |
|---------|----------|-----|
| `qresearch gemini` | Gemini | Skill `gemini-research` or `pnpm research:op --query "..."` |
| `qresearch perplexity` | Perplexity | Skill `perplexity-research` → MCP tools |
| `qresearch` (no suffix) | Gemini (default) | Same as `qresearch gemini` |

Keys: `gemini` + `perplexity` items in vault. Check: `pnpm env:op-check`. Relaunch Cursor: `op run --env-file=.env.1password -- open -a Cursor .`

**Greptile setup:** `docs/guides/greptile-setup.md`

